i don't know if it's become sort of a  cheesy line to say that a certain show  or anime in some way changed you or  helped you through a tough time in your  life the profound idea that a piece of  entertainment could have such a tangible  effect that it helps shapes you and even  if you may change grow older grow more  mature you still carry a piece of it  with you years after you watch it  i'm sure many of you have one or two  things that have done that for you but  in anime i don't think there's a  franchise that has touched and  influenced as big of an audience as  evangelion evangelion is quite possibly  my favorite anime of all time or at  least it's the one i've carried with me  for the longest and i know that's not  really a hot take considering this is  arguably the most influential anime of  all time but i still do think it's a  series every anime fan needs to  experience at least once in their lives  not because i think everyone will  instantly love it as a universally  acclaimed masterpiece but because it's  such a profoundly powerful and intimate  piece of media that if by chance you do  come out of this resonating with a  character or a scene or maybe just a  single line  it'll stick with you for a very very  long time  it's touched many lives in a way no  other piece of media has or ever will  and i think it'd be a massive shame if  there was even a chance of anyone  depriving themselves of that experience  i say this but i actually hated it the  first two times i watched it because i  think the worst thing that ava does is  that it genuinely builds up this  interesting world and mystery and it  just sets the wrong expectations i  remember thinking man this is such a  cool world i can't wait till they  explain where the angels come from what  the dead sea scrolls are the lands of  longinus what's gonna happen to the  characters and how are they gonna  resolve all their problems and then  none of that happened the ending that  was meant to conclude it did the  opposite the tv series ending at the  time felt like a low budget therapy  session tacked on because the studio ran  out of money and the end of evangelion  movie was to me a  self-masturbatory pretentious mind [ __ ]  that left me less satisfied than when i  started it i came into ava expecting a  traditional story and i went out  confused and unfulfilled i had so many  questions and zero answers i was angry  that i had gotten invested in the series  in the first place i spent days  researching reading explanations getting  into online arguments and i left even  more confused i could not understand how  a series like this got the critical  claim that it did and that's how it was  for me for the longest time  then  years later i entered the darkest period  of my life  several massive things happened to me  and i was in the worst mental state i'd  ever been in and ever have been in still  nothing could pick me up from this well  i'd fallen into my favorite anime lost  their magic games were no longer fun  everything just kind of felt meaningless  and for some reason i decided to put on  evangelion because hell  why the [ __ ] not right this time though  something just clicked i no longer cared  about the mysteries or the lore of the  world i saw broken people trying to find  value in who they were i saw pieces of  myself spread out in every character and  the fever dream artsy sequences i  dismissed as pretentious before somehow  made sense  it was like someone had laid out my  jumbled fractured stream of  consciousness and put it on screen  for the first time i actually started to  understand it and by understand i don't  just mean that i suddenly had an  epiphany that allowed me to comprehend  every small line in detail but it felt  like on some level i could empathize  with what these characters were feeling  with what the creator was trying to say  it felt like someone understood the pain  i was going through and in a way that  gave me comfort  to me in some twisted way it made me  feel like i might have been suffering  but at least there was someone out there  who could empathize with this pain i was  feeling someone else had felt what i was  feeling right now  my life wasn't suddenly cured but a lot  of things just mentally clicked together  and  at least for a period  it gave me a sense of tranquility  and i think that's the real power of  evangelion  when people say you don't get evangelion  i used to think that it was a  pretentious way of attacking my  intelligence that i somehow couldn't  comprehend  what was going on but now i just think  it just means that you don't resonate  with the emotions being portrayed on  screen because to me there's no real way  you can truly understand ava i've  watched a lot of people far smarter and  more attentive than i ever will be  analyze every single character broken  down its themes and symbolism spent  hours upon hours breaking down every  single part of this franchise and i  still  don't fully understand ava but i'm fine  with that because i think by design i  don't know if it's even meant to be  something you can comprehend in a  traditional sense  it's quite well known that the creator  hideakiano was in an awful state of mind  when he made it and i can never ignore  this because i remember during that  period in my life little if anything  made sense at all emotions don't always  make sense and that's what i feel from  this show i don't see someone trying to  lay out a coherent narrative meant to be  understood i see a guttural cry for help  i see someone trying so desperately to  find resolution to their own internal  struggles more than any other series  i've seen this feels like someone laying  their feelings bare in front of us for  no other purpose other than the  catharsis of expressing themselves and  this is something i can personally  relate to i think the most powerful  thing i've ever made to date is this amv  called reflections of despair  it's still on youtube now but it's  something that i made during that dark  period and i made it for no reason other  than  i just needed to i needed to vent i  needed to put my pain into something i  didn't have anyone to talk to i didn't  have anyone to pick me up so i sat in my  room alone for two days straight putting  my emotions into the editing timeline of  this video  to me it was my way of crying for help  i was screaming in total silence  i am still incredibly proud of this amv  even if i don't recognize the person who  made it sure i know i did i literally  remember doing it but i couldn't  recreate something like this even if i  tried for better or worse i'm thankfully  in a much better place now and looking  back at this i don't know what i was  trying to say i don't know why i picked  the lines i did why i chose these scenes  or why i use this song all i know is  that  it felt right  at the time i realized this isn't  comparable to making a full tv series  but this is what i feel from every  iteration of ava perhaps anno did know  exactly what he wanted to say perhaps he  didn't but what i always feel is the  catharsis of his raw unbridled emotions  etched into the show it's so strongly  imbued with these emotions that if  you've ever related even just a little  bit it's impossible to not have some  kind of guttural reaction to it to use  it as a springboard to reflect on  yourself  every time i've watched evangelion i've  come out with something new and there's  just something special about a series  that can teach me something new about  myself every single time i watch it if  there was one thing i never got from ava  however it was that feeling of a  satisfying end at least naturally as you  grow older you realize that not  everything in life has a clean ending  not everything has a perfect solution  and that's fine  sometimes you just learn to live with it  and move on and that's exactly what  happens with me and ava which brings me  to my motivation of making this video in  the first place which is the final  evangelion film that just got its  release worldwide avangelion 3.0 plus  1.0 my hype for the final ava movie died  a long time ago at first i was giddy at  the possibility of having a proper  ending and then three films took five  years to make and then after that one  year passed  then two years then five years and now  almost 10 years after 3.0 came out my  initial reaction to it getting released  was  oh  it's out by this point in life i had  made peace with the franchise i could  have gotten no more ava in my life at  all and i would have been completely  fine with it i was no longer invested  enough to even care how it concluded  which is why i'm so blindsided by how  much this movie meant for me this didn't  just feel like 9 years in the making it  felt like 26 years in the making and i  can't even begin to describe the  cathartic release of feeling what i  never got to feel over half my lifetime  ago now when i first watched ava  closure  was it the perfect movie no  was every little thing resolved no was  it even my favorite ending no but it was  one that i'd forgotten that i was  waiting for i have no shame in admitting  that i didn't understand most of what  was going on but like i've said to me  ava was never a series about the perfect  narrative understanding every plot point  or tying up all loose ends it was about  emotional resonance and what resonated  with me was someone who had truly found  a way to move past their inner demons in  the original eva shinji learned to  accept who he was and love himself and  every ending kind of replicates that  same sentiment but this time it felt  different because it really felt like  the person behind him saying it  had time to properly believe it you  don't just wake up one day and be okay  with the world you don't just take one  pill and wish goodbye to depression you  don't just have one pep talk  and realize that everything that was  broken about you  is now fixed  so  experiencing the work of the same guy  who made ava 26 years later and not just  seeing but actually feeling a completely  different person retelling the story a  happier person exuding through this  final ending i  actually couldn't be more delighted i  couldn't be happier that someone like me  had  found a way to move on i don't know how  i could possibly convey the feeling of  having a franchise that meant so much to  you that stuck with you for years that  you'd made peace with that you thought  would always be there  coming to an end  i felt happy that i got to experience  such an amazing journey in the first  place i felt sad because i felt like i  was finally putting an aspect of my  younger self to rest for good i felt  empty because this was it this was truly  the end  but most of all i felt fulfilled  in a way only ava could make me feel  in the end to me ava was a passionate  way for one man to lay his raw emotions  and ideas out there it's the story of a  broken man on his journey to solace as a  fan you view this journey through foggy  glasses you spend your time figuring out  where he was going with all this you  guess second guess analyze creep in for  a closer look research analyze over  every detail ponder over whether it  means anything at all question why you  give a damn in the first place only to  realize that in the end  it meant something to you  something about it spoke to you  that's just the baggage that came with  being an ava fan because whatever  message you take from the franchise from  the endings from any of the iterations  it is and always will be  your own  this is a series that will probably  stick with me for the rest of my life  but i've grown up and moved on to a  world without ava even so i couldn't be  more thankful that i was given one last  opportunity to properly put a rest to  that part of my life and in the end  i don't think there's anything more i  can say  other than  goodbye  and thank you  all  of evangelion  [Music]  you

